OFF-STAGE EVENTS
GUIDELINES

DEBATE
GUIDELINES

• Duration: 4–5 minutes
• Participants: Each department shall be represented by one team consisting of two participants.
• Language: English and Malayalam will be conducted as separate competitions.
• The debate will be conducted on the spot based on the given topic/idea.
• The topic will be provided to the participants at the venue, and they must prepare accordingly.
• One team shall speak in favour of the topic, while the other shall speak against the topic.
• The language used during the competition must be professional, appropriate, and respectful.
• Participants must maintain proper decorum while presenting their arguments.
• Personal remarks, offensive language, abusive expressions, or inappropriate content will not be permitted.
• Participants will be judged based on content, clarity of arguments, presentation, relevance, confidence, and overall debating skills.

QUIZ
GUIDELINES

• Team: 2 participants.
• Questions will be based on General Knowledge & Current Affairs.
• The quiz will consist of multiple rounds.
• Mobile phones and electronic devices are not allowed.
• No prompting or external assistance is permitted.
• Tie-breaker will be conducted if required.
• The Quizmaster’s decision will be final.
• Participants must maintain discipline and decorum.

AKSHARASHLOKA
GUIDELINES

• Individual participation.
• Repetition of previously recited verses is not allowed.
• Time limit: As decided by the organisers.
• Failure to continue within the allotted time may result in elimination.
• The judges’ decision shall be final and binding.

KAVYAKELI
GUIDELINES

• Individual participation.
• Performance must be completed within the allotted time.
• No prompting or external assistance is allowed.
• The judges’ decision shall be final and binding.

JUST A MINUTE
GUIDELINES

• Individual participation.
• Language: English.
• The topic will be given on the spot.
• Participants must speak continuously for one minute.
• Repetition, hesitation, and deviation from the topic are not allowed.
• The judges’ decision shall be final and binding.

RANGOLI
GUIDELINES

• Participation: Individual.
• Maximum Duration: 2½ hours.
• Participants must bring all required materials themselves.
• Rangoli may be created using freehand designs or with drawing tools.
• Only colour powder may be used.
• Adhesive materials are strictly prohibited.
• Rangoli must be created only at the designated spot provided for the competition.

WALL PAINTING
GUIDELINES

• Team participation – 2 members per team.
• Maximum duration: 2 hours.
• The wall and painting area will be allotted by the organisers.
• Participants must bring all required painting materials and drawing tools themselves.
• Only colour paints may be used.
• The design must be created on the spot based on the given theme/topic.
• Pre-drawn designs, stencils, or printed materials are not allowed.
• Participants must maintain cleanliness and avoid damaging the surroundings.
• The artwork must be completed within the allotted time.
• Judges’ decision shall be final and binding.

